{"id": "EUVD-2026-70341", "enisaUuid": "b69777b6-81f5-377e-89e9-d693d8ee61cd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nserial: amba-pl011: synchronize DMA teardown\n\ndmaengine_terminate_all() does not wait for a running callback, so the TX\ncallback can still touch the TX buffer after it is freed. The RX poll\ntimer reads the RX buffers without the port lock.\n\nSwitch to dmaengine_terminate_sync() and delete the RX timer before\nfreeing the buffers.", "datePublished": "2026-09-03T08:21:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:26:36", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a38fae9d212e2d3ed5e9ec0ef773f8c0a27fb76e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/44bd0ecc3444882d08ecfbc2b2418d2f463d3186", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f70c9d4fba46463a5b1c7b3ee9ee3b40c90dac03", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c8c8e895f65fbf71ea6224e27cf8dab91b776e0d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9f6989e477f03a4721d34bb4b09b17accd40283e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5974cb66681eac367107b05924744d7e3b49d41c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fdfb46c387241b4eddd36d746793764413285913", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/440915499231e9db1c361aa45bb702e8fd3b4a32"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j4vm-79j3-8jfc", "CVE-2026-80737"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0140df52-0cd2-3978-a0bb-86a8a23f32cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ead76f329f777c7301e0a5456a0a1c7a081570bd <9f6989e477f03a4721d34bb4b09b17accd40283e"}, {"id": "1dbb1404-978e-3c51-9bb8-a1571a6fd4e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.154"}, {"id": "2b8d4ae9-ffde-357f-bee5-d05d36578763", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ead76f329f777c7301e0a5456a0a1c7a081570bd <5974cb66681eac367107b05924744d7e3b49d41c"}, {"id"